  "claim": "After the bounded viewMode/focus replay, Target121 u22106 retains ten genuine owner-added rows and six build-macro rows. The first allowed key is the smallest adjacency-closed next unit: its policy-filter declaration, blocked warning, and sole spread consumer form one three-statement graph whose identifier-normalized tokens are byte-for-byte descriptor-identical in complete Target120 u22004 and Target121 u22106. Both accepted main.tsx source states already contain that exact graph in run, so no source replay is warranted. This case admits only the first allowed key at 13797608..13797615. The later allowed return branch and the other eight genuine rows remain explicit deferred identities; six VERSION/BUILD_TIME/GIT_SHA rows remain separately classified build macros.",
